WEBVTT

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.630
Finally found you.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:18.240
First Lt. Messer's back.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.460
Right.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.350
Chaos Ragna division,

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.940
salute First Lt. Messer Ihlefeld!

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.030
We've only got one shot at love,

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.880
so let's have fun inside of you

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.740
Let's share a selfish kiss

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.540
The petals of this flower fall in the wind

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:16.010
The stars are more than I could count

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:19.550
I could place all the blame on you,

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.300
swallowing back my tears,

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.140
but I can't tell anyone about how my heart races

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.650
Until it all breaks apart

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.830
Until you can take flight

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:35.320
(To the ends)

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:36.200
Deep in my heart

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.740
There is a prayer

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.660
Just feel, just believe

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.760
and speed through it all

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.920
We've only got one shot at love,

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.670
so let's have fun inside of you

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:57.260
Let's share a kiss faster than light, just wait for me

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.890
I'll leave my body behind

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:02.890
I'll leave my heart beating hard

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:08.320
I'll break free from these chains holding me down

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:15.030
Just come get me, in my purest form

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:28.120
Brainwaves, vitals, and neural responses all normal.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.880
Everything seems fine regardless of what test we run.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.790
Did you really see it?

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:38.720
While I was singing, I suddenly saw this weird place.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.960
It was so open and cold...

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.430
I was really scared.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.850
They saw right into us. All the way.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.980
Some brain hackers got into your consciousness?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.700
Barging in without even saying hello...

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.240
That's one way to get on my bad side.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.670
But who?

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.160
The Wind Singer.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.500
The Wind Singer?

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.740
So Mikumo and Freyja made contact with the Wind Singer?

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:14.880
Yes.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:21.800
During the last battle, we detected abnormal bio-fold values around the two of them.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.760
We're still analyzing the data,

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:30.980
but it appears that the Protoculture ruins
caused the singers to interfere with one another.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:37.530
The power the song of the wind
holds might shake the entire galaxy.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.490
By the way, Kaname...

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.060
Yes?

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:47.160
Are you sure you don't want to take a day or two off?

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.710
I'm fine. Thanks for your concern.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.880
Okay, then...

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.380
What about yourself, captain?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.300
I'll manage.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.190
This is the problem.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.630
Yeah.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.150
What is?

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.580
Look at that.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.390
He managed to shoot the cockpit,

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.450
and hit precisely the heart of the pilot.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.990
What a stroke of bad luck.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:37.000
Right. No human could pull that off.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.440
He aimed for it.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.080
That damned White Knight...

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:52.680
The energy transfer circuits have been
overloaded, so we'll just give you a new machine.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.120
Thanks.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.790
No surprise.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:00.520
That was quite a battle to behold.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.650
He was nowhere even close to Lord Keith's level.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:10.280
It is but natural that some lowlife challenging the White Knight would meet his fate.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.750
Lord Keith?

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.750
Could you wake such a wind?

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.960
What did I say?

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:31.940
Your rune.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.070
Everything was burning.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.260
Only flames and heat.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.860
Was that Windermere?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.080
I'm terribly sorry.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:53.070
The technology of the Protoculture and its effects are still not fully understood.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:00.040
You must be tired. Please rest.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.470
The resonance of the fold waves is increasing.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.300
I have arrived.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.270
Come.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:18.250
Your Majesty.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:23.520
Berger, why are you here?

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.280
I have news for His Majesty.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.410
The capabilities of the Protoculture's great legacy, Sigur Valens,

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:35.660
have been analyzed up to 60%.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.870
It can now be activated.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:38.920
What?!

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:42.500
Roid, alert all forces.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.690
We are mobilizing.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.550
Do you intend to go yourself, Your Majesty?

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.610
You mustn't in your condition!

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.050
The wind is crying.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.020
None of it rings from your rune.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:07:00.040
You are hiding your own uncertainties.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.980
Do you fear for Heinz?

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:06.480
He felt the enemy's song, has he not?

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.650
How do you know?

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.200
I could feel the disturbance of his wind in my rune.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:19.910
If this so-called Walküre is this powerful,
we must strike with matching preparations.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:24.380
Henceforth, I will personally take control of all our forces.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.360
Your Majesty.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:36.890
Why are you so concerned about the well-being of Prince Heinz?

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:39.500
It is my duty as his retainer.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:42.160
Even against the will of His Majesty?

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:45.060
He is the Wind Singer.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:51.360
The great Protoculture bestowed that gift upon us Windermereans.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:56.910
Prince Heinz might become the king of all Protoculture.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.290
The Protoculture again...

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:04.750
The power of the ruins, the song of the wind, the water and the apples,

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.050
are all things they gave to us.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:11.210
I recognize your achievements in making use of all that.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:14.340
But you're forgetting something important.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.760
What exactly?

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.580
Our lives are short.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.890
We have no time.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.980
Did we not vow?

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:28.300
Me from the skies, and you with your wings folded from the ground,

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:34.110
would make this nation strong
and free it from its tainted past.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.950
I still feel the same.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.760
I see.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:42.620
However, you were too slow.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.730
Too slow?

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:52.630
Soon, time itself will not matter.

00:08:58.090 --> 00:08:59.760
Messer...

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:06.230
He told some movers to get rid all of his stuff.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.440
Guess he was always prepared to die or something.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.020
That's just like him.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.400
We have no time to mourn.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:19.000
We need to fill the gap he left and fast.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:23.870
We'll probably get someone
from the Alpha or Beta Platoons.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.960
Someone to replace him?

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.370
You look unhappy.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:34.440
The Delta Platoon lost 37% of its combat potential.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.210
Can you cover that by yourself?

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:39.640
Scared?

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.480
Windermere's not gonna wait.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.200
I know.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:48.770
Hayate!

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.520
Let him be.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.940
It's probably the first time he lost a comrade.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.160
Music is mystery!

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.660
Music is life!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.440
Music is energy!

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:03.870
Music is hope!

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:07.000
Keep it up! In the end, it all comes down to stamina!

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:07.930
Keep it up!

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:09.470
Music is life!

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:10.710
Music is energy!

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.730
Music is hope!

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:14.950
If we were stronger, we might've saved him.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.190
Music is love!

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.040
Music is mystery!

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.420
Music is life!

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.880
Music is energy!

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.760
Dammit!

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.760
Music is hope!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.400
Music is love!

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:23.840
Music is mystery!

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.620
Music is life!

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:26.930
Dammit!

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:26.930
Music is energy!

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:30.650
Sending visualization to the main monitor.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:33.910
What's this?

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:39.570
The coordinates of the Protoculture ruins annexed by Windermere so far.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:45.910
And these are the places that reported hearing the song during the last battle.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:50.190
It could be heard on all planets with ruins?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:51.080
No.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.090
Even on planets without them?!

00:10:55.270 --> 00:11:01.970
Furthermore, analysis of the ruins in the globular cluster shows

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:08.680
that the lines connecting them form a field that covers all the planets.

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:10.890
Which means...

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:13.400
This is what the Windermereans were after.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:17.150
Shall the ruins on Al Shahal and Ragna fall,

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:21.680
they could put all 8 billion inhabitants of the cluster under mind control.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:26.110
They'll be coming, and it'll be soon.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:28.160
We need reinforcements.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.570
I've already asked Lady M.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.410
Now, we pray they make it in time.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:38.670
They took everything from Windermere on that day.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.620
Our wind. Our lives. Our pride.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:46.530
That shameful day our land was scarred.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:49.350
But the days of shame will soon be over.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.720
Today, we mobilize all our forces

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.940
to annihilate the earthlings and those allied with them.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.150
We will retake all the ruins

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:01.110
and secure the Starwind sector.

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:08.330
We, the true inheritors of the Protoculture, shall free the globular cluster!

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:12.060
May the wind grant us glory!

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:36.540
Arise, Sigur Valens!

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.270
The target is Al Shahal!

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:06.870
Has it really been revived?

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:09.760
It is no dream, Lord Roid.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:13.960
The heritage of the Protoculture, this ship you excavated,

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:18.730
the Sigur Valens, now takes on the skies again.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:23.570
We should thank His Majesty for allowing us on board.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:31.290
That is the loss of Windermere.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:37.220
The fight shall not be over until we reclaim all that was lost there,

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:40.540
Heinz Nehrich Windermere.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:43.130
As you say, Your Majesty.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:53.350
Hayate!

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.100
You're late!

00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.290
We're here!

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:00.770
Me too!

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:02.650
Hey, Hayate.

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:04.510
Took you long enough.

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.270
What took you so long?

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:07.790
Hey, Haya-Haya.

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:09.270
What are you doing?

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:10.410
You can't tell?

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.370
We're returning him to the jellyfish.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.740
Excuse me?

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:14.520
Yeah.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:15.870
Look!

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.740
Tadada!

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:20.960
What d'you think? Isn't it cool?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.000
It's a bit ugly but so cute!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.170
Heck, yeah!

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:31.760
On Ragna, we believe that the spirits of the dead
return to the sea and turn into shining jellyfishes.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:36.480
They swim in the sea and their pains are eased over time.

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:39.000
Once all their pain is gone, they are reborn.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:45.780
In order for them to turn into jellyfish, we put their souls on a ship and send them off at sea.

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:48.490
We drink and sing in remembrance.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:53.850
I was gonna explain, but you ran off by yourself.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:55.810
Everyone's here?

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:57.790
Let's get wasted tonight!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.820
My contribution.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.000
Ah, thank—

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.930
Wait, is this 20-year-old banana sake?!

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:05.710
Where did you get this baby from?!

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:09.330
I wanted to drink it with Messer some day.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:16.350
Let's drink in his stead.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:18.190
You're only drinking for yourself.

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:18.930
What?!

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:24.400
What was that?

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.320
That was lame!

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.580
Not really!

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:38.010
When I come here, I recall

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:49.280
the days where all we did was dream

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:57.890
The lingering wind from the stars

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:08.520
takes me back to days past

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:15.730
Under the wild blue sky

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.670
What's wrong?

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:21.280
It was just the two of us

00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:23.330
We should've told the others about the Lieutenant's illness.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:28.020
We shared smiles and dreams of a distant future

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:32.080
If he was moved to another division sooner, things may have turned out otherwise.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:34.380
Don't worry, I didn't forget

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:35.560
I think it's because of what I said to him.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:38.840
the promise we made back then

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.770
I talked to Messer the other day.

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:44.500
With the same power and the same speed

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.900
I told him I never think about the future.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:49.070
I knew he wasn't okay back then.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:52.380
We're still dreaming. Remember 16.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.780
Me too.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:59.660
If I hadn't let him return to the sky...

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:01.140
Captain...

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:07.580
But if it wasn't for him, the Delta Platoon wouldn't have made it this far either.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.050
Yeah.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:11.800
Sorry for running so late.

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:16.180
We found this in the Lieutenant's unit.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:21.570
We wanted to check if it was a private item of his, but it's apparently a flight log.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:25.950
Let's see...

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.620
August 6th.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:29.060
Second Lt. Chuck Mustang.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:32.750
Used too much propellant at high altitude.

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:34.150
August 16th.

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:37.020
Second Lt. Mirage Farina Jenius.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:40.120
Only during rapid descends, she tends to ease the pitch of her plane.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.620
August 19th.

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:45.100
Sgt. Hayate Immelmann.

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:48.580
His use of the engine during a turn was too careless.

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.610
August 21st.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:55.050
During the Immelmann dance,
his unit skewed toward the left.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:59.500
It must be a minuscule delay due to using his non-dominant leg.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:03.500
What an attention to detail...

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:09.160
He must've loved flying.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:13.270
I love singing.

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:22.160
I love to watch Walküre—Mikumo,
Kaname, Makina, and Reina—sing.

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:25.240
Messer must've felt the same way about you all.

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.050
He must've.

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:30.830
He wouldn't have watched
you all so closely otherwise.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:35.920
I see. His love for flying is what
made him so beautiful in the air.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.090
That's why it was so enthralling to us.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:46.930
He always said you had nothing in your head.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.240
At least quote him correctly!

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:50.500
He used to say he flies as if
he's got nothing else in his head.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:51.940
Oh, right.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:55.580
And also that Mirage is clumsy and always serious,

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:58.560
but that she's straightforward in a good way.

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:00.550
Really?

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:03.290
He never told us anything like that.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:06.410
He might've been trying to keep his distances.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:11.580
Because if he got too close, you wouldn't be able to finish him off if he lost control.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:19.470
And we were supposed to figure that out?

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:25.060
Don't just look all smart as if you knew everything!

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:33.180
Let's send him off.

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:40.600
One, two...

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:59.920
You couldn't catch up, so you always

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:09.640
looked up at something from here

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:01.740
Mikumo?

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:17.550
Some things vanish if you reach them

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:17.430
I can't just gobble down jellyfish anymore.

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:19.480
I might be eating Messer.

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:29.290
You've been hiding your countless tears too

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:28.760
You were right, captain.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:32.260
I was scared by Messer's death.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:37.560
Your eyes were so honest and pure,

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:36.150
And that there was someone
stronger than him out there.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:39.460
And that I could do nothing about it.

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:48.430
but you never saw this world that way

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:43.480
I've made up my mind.

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:45.640
We don't need any replacements.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.830
I'll fly Messer's share too.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:57.400
You don't have to chase your dreams alone

00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:06.300
The invisible wind will help you

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:15.110
I feel I can fly so far, so high

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:14.140
He shone brighter than anyone else on that day.

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:24.880
just please don't let go of my hand

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:18.220
You too, Kaname.

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:23.130
Freyja's not your only rival.

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:26.970
There are people who hold my songs dear.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:31.720
So I'm going to sing stronger than anyone else.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:45.300
You don't have to chase your dreams alone

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:53.870
The invisible wind will help you

00:21:53.870 --> 00:22:02.730
I feel I can fly so far, so high

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:14.130
just please don't let go of my hand

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:15.990
(Your dreams alone...)

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:24.620
(Invisible wind...)

00:22:28.330 --> 00:22:34.240
Love ripples

00:22:52.740 --> 00:22:58.880
Mission 11: Jellyfish Reminiscence

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:02.400
Planet Al Shahal

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:05.580
What's happening?

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:07.040
De-fold signals!

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:08.360
We're detecting something immense!

00:23:08.590 --> 00:23:10.610
It's a ship, but...

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.010
The wind is blowing.

00:23:20.010 --> 00:23:22.630
Let us begin, Heinz!

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:24.340
Yes.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:29.800
All ships, arm main turrets!

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:33.760
Fire!

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:39.850
Next time: King of the Wind
